## Request

Build one declarative release-capability inventory and a thin convergence planner over existing
guarded domain operations. The planner owns dependency ordering, action classification, stale-state
refusal, durable bounded journaling, idempotent resume, and agreement verification. It must not
become a second migration engine or weaken the authority, archive, approval, rollback, or token
contracts delivered by M1 and existing domain migrations.

Add disposable representative SQLite probes for configured interactive and background Python
runtimes. Report read health separately from guarded mutation readiness, including the issue #66
Python 3.11.2 / SQLite 3.39.4 `trusted_schema=OFF` trigger failure as a controlled incompatibility
with the exact interpreter remediation. Feed that truth into Doctor and convergence summaries.

Extend conversion integrity to unambiguous relationship extraction and immutable-ID compatibility.
Imported deterministic UUIDv5 document identities must be valid outcome and relationship targets;
ambiguity must remain an explicit finding. Keep schema migration, required compatibility backfill,
and optional semantic enrichment as separate named action classes, and never create readiness,
planning history, or historical outcomes merely to make validation pass.

Prove fresh, partial, failed, deferred, interrupted, resumed, repeated, stale-token, rollback, and
dirty-state behavior in disposable fixtures. Stop after focused implementation proof, strict Doctor,
configured development-lane verification, exact Work2 candidate registration, and a durable Hybrid
checkpoint. Do not publish, tag, release, synchronize installed clients, close issue #66, begin M3,
or mutate the `workpc` firmware workspace in this campaign.

