## Result

The 0.53.0 candidate now ships a versioned release-capability inventory and a thin planner that
orders the existing guarded schema migrations, required compatibility backfills, and optional
semantic enrichment without becoming another migration engine. Fresh and existing eligible Git
workspaces converge through the installer and updater; non-Git paths remain coherently deferred.
Plans bind project, release inventory, authority, database revision and digest, runtimes, work
content, and Git state, while a bounded hash-chained journal supports idempotent resume.

Disposable probes distinguish read health from actual guarded writes for both interactive and
background runtimes. The issue #66 Python 3.11.2 / SQLite 3.39.4 trusted-schema trigger failure is
now classified as SQLITE_TRUSTED_SCHEMA_TRIGGER_UNSAFE with an interpreter-upgrade action. Doctor
reports read and mutation readiness separately. Updater rollback restores the exact prior Hybrid
database or removes a newly created shadow database.

Conversion now extracts only unambiguous explicit document-header relationships using stable
identities. Deterministic UUIDv5 imported artifacts are accepted as outcome origins and
relationship targets while outcome-domain row identities remain UUIDv4. The canonical workspace
backfilled 71 relationships with zero findings and repeated planning reported complete parity.
Document-authority conversion remains one explicit archived decision, and no readiness, planning
history, or historical outcome is fabricated.

